  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23605391.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Salmonid Disk Tagging Aboard the R/V Wakatake maru in the Central North Pacific Ocean and Bering Sea during the Summer of 2002 (BASIS Japan)",
  "description": "The Wakatake maru (666 gross tons) departed Kushiro on June 8, 2002 and returned on July 21, 2002. There were 28 experimental fishing stations during the cruise. Nineteen fishing stations were located in the vicinity of 180º longitude from 41ºN to 58º30メN latitude, and nine operations were conducted in the international waters of the central Bering Sea. Live salmon caught in a healthy condition were put into a recovery tank soon after removal from the longline. Fish were tagged with two disk tags issued by the Fisheries Agency of Japan (JFA) and the Fisheries Research Institute, University of Washington (FRI). Both disk tags were placed on one plastic cinch strap and applied to the fish anterior to the dorsal fin. The fork length was measured and two scales were collected before the fish was released to the sea. A total of 1042 tagged salmonids were released to the North Pacific Ocean (n = 42) and Bering Sea (n = 1000). The releases included 974 chum, 28 sockeye, 21 chinook, 15 coho, 2 pink salmon, and 2 steelhead trout. Of these fish, 51 salmon at St.27 and 28 were released with only JFA disk tag because we exhausted our supply of FRI disk tags at St.27. [Reference: Tanaka, H, N. Davis, T. Onuma, M. Yamada, Y. Yamamoto, and S. Tsuchiya. 2002. International salmon research aboard the R/V Wakatake maru in the central North Pacific Ocean and Bering Sea during the summer of 2002. (NPAFC Doc. 622). 21 p. Hokkaido National Fisheries Research Institute, Fisheries Research Agency, 116 Katsurakoi, Kushiro 085-0802, Japan.] This report is available at http://www.npafc.org/BASIS/622(Japan).pdf\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To monitor the stock condition of salmon ( Oncorhynchus spp.) in the central North Pacific Ocean and Bering Sea.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23605392",
